## Proof

- **${n_tests} tests** (`pytest`): tag mapping and priority, bank revenue, two-step dedupe, restatement audit, primary keys, Massachusetts universe, fiscal calendar, every SQL check runs.
- **${n_checks} SQL data-quality checks** run on every build; failures are kept visible in [`output/dq_results.csv`](output/dq_results.csv), not suppressed.
- **One command:** `make` builds the warehouse and runs the tests; from cache the pipeline takes a few seconds.
- **Data:** [SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts](https://www.sec.gov/edgar/sec-api-documentation) (${raw_mb} MB) and SEC submissions, declared User-Agent, throttled to 5 requests per second.
- **Deterministic:** SHA-256 of every raw file recorded in `data/raw/manifest.json`; `run.py --offline` rebuilds from the cache only. Data as of ${run_date}.

